# MoviePilot never-proxy set (bandwidth guard)
# Updated: 2026-08-04
#
# Consumer: server-side sing-box (ai2americaproxy) NOPROXY_RULE_URL.
# Evaluated BEFORE every acceleration list, so a match here always wins.
#
# Purpose: the NAS sits behind this proxy, and the upstream US node is metered.
# This file is the hard stop for traffic whose size is unbounded — downloads,
# cloud drives, media streams, container images, OS packages. Anything that
# should never be able to burn upstream quota belongs here, not in a comment.
#
# In the Quantumult X profile this list is registered with enabled=false: the
# phone profile already ends in FINAL,Proxy plus GEOIP,CN,Direct, and forcing
# these domains direct there would only break them on mobile networks.
#
# Adding to this file is always safe. The server config ends in final=direct,
# so a domain listed here falls back to the server's own direct egress.

# ========= BitTorrent trackers =========
# Belt and braces only: tracker announces are issued by qBittorrent/Transmission,
# which do not use this proxy, and each announce is kilobyte-scale anyway.
# Deliberately NOT a HOST-KEYWORD,tracker rule — that also swallows
# origin-tracker.githubusercontent.com, which the AI list needs accelerated.
HOST-SUFFIX,opentrackr.org,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,openbittorrent.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,torrent.eu.org,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,demonii.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,leechers-paradise.org,Direct

# ========= Download clients =========
HOST-SUFFIX,qbittorrent.org,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,transmissionbt.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,xunlei.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,thunderurl.com,Direct

# ========= GitHub release-asset CDNs =========
# MoviePilot's plugin market pulls individual files from raw.githubusercontent.com
# and never needs release assets, while a single asset can be hundreds of MB.
# If some plugin genuinely needs one, move that host into moviepilot.list.
HOST,objects.githubusercontent.com,Direct
HOST,release-assets.githubusercontent.com,Direct
HOST,github-releases.githubusercontent.com,Direct

# ========= Container registries =========
# Image pulls are the single largest traffic source on a NAS. Use a domestic
# registry mirror on the NAS instead of routing these through the proxy.
HOST-SUFFIX,docker.io,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,docker.com,Direct
HOST,production.cloudflare.docker.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,ghcr.io,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,gcr.io,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,quay.io,Direct

# ========= Cloud drives used by MoviePilot plugins =========
HOST-SUFFIX,aliyundrive.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,alipan.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,aliyuncs.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,115.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,115cdn.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,anxia.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,quark.cn,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,baidupcs.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,pcs.baidu.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,pikpak.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,mypikpak.com,Direct

# ========= Overseas cloud drives =========
HOST-SUFFIX,dropbox.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,dropboxusercontent.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,onedrive.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,1drv.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,sharepoint.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,teracloud.jp,Direct

# ========= Local and self-hosted media servers =========
# *.plex.direct resolves to a LAN address; routing it out would break playback.
HOST-SUFFIX,plex.direct,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,emby.media,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,jellyfin.org,Direct

# ========= Domestic sites — never need a US exit =========
HOST-SUFFIX,cn,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,douban.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,doubanio.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,bilibili.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,hdslb.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,iqiyi.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,youku.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,mgtv.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,qq.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,myqcloud.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,aliyun.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,tencentcloud.com,Direct

# ========= OS packages, NAS firmware, package registries =========
HOST-SUFFIX,debian.org,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,ubuntu.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,alpinelinux.org,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,npmjs.org,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,npmmirror.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,synology.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,qnap.com,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,ugreen.com,Direct

# ========= Speed tests =========
HOST-KEYWORD,speedtest,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,ooklaserver.net,Direct

# ========= Private networks =========
# Only meaningful for the Quantumult X client, where FINAL is Proxy. The server
# config already ends in final=direct, so these are a no-op there and the
# generator skips IP rules entirely.
IP-CIDR,10.0.0.0/8,Direct,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,172.16.0.0/12,Direct,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,192.168.0.0/16,Direct,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,127.0.0.0/8,Direct,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,100.64.0.0/10,Direct,no-resolve
HOST-SUFFIX,local,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,lan,Direct
HOST-SUFFIX,internal,Direct
